# Osmium Sound — where the U-Boot environment lives, for fw_printenv/fw_setenv
# (libubootenv). RAUC's u-boot backend shells out to these to read BOOT_ORDER
# and to reset/clear BOOT_<slot>_LEFT on mark-good/mark-bad.
#
# The environment is a single 16 KiB `uboot.env` file on the FAT boot
# partition, which the Pi firmware + U-Boot read first and which Debian mounts
# at /boot/firmware. It must be mounted for fw_setenv to work — hifi-rauc-config
# mounts it early at boot (the boot partition is this fork's "ESP").
#
# 🚨 The 0x4000 size must match the U-Boot build's CONFIG_ENV_SIZE and the
# mkenvimage size used in build-image-pi3.sh. Verify on real hardware.
#
# device/file            offset   env-size
/boot/firmware/uboot.env 0x0000   0x4000
